WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:03.650
- [Interviewer] All
right, Jason and Tasha.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.600
Jason and Tasha where are you guys from?

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.492
- [Jason] Missouri.

00:00:06.492 --> 00:00:07.325
- [Tasha] We're from Missouri.

00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:08.910
- [Interviewer] And you guys are married?

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.037
- [Tasha] No, we were
together for four years.

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:12.150
We're pretty much married.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.390
- [Interviewer] Then, tell
me about how you grew up.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.223
Jason.

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:19.160
- I grew up with a biker as a father,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.700
and mom wasn't around,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.049
when I didn't meet her.

00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:24.610
We were doing drugs immediately.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:29.550
So I grew up in a environment
where drugs were accepted

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.470
and passed around as children.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.100
So we grew up kind of fast.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.100
- [Interviewer] So drugs
came into your life-

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.250
- Really early, about 13
years old, I was doing drugs.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.083
- [Interviewer] What kind of stuff?

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.210
- Like heroin was my first addiction.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.410
Yeah, was well strong
opiates, morphine, Oxycontin.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.350
And then it switched to heroin
later on when I ran out.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.510
But-

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.263
- [Interviewer] And how would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.670
- Traumatic.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.503
Yeah.

00:00:58.503 --> 00:00:59.940
- [Interviewer] What kind
of stuff was going on?

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.793
- Violence.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.453
Like a lot of violence, a lot of drugs,

00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:10.287
a lot of in and out of state custody

00:01:12.247 --> 00:01:14.327
and kidnappings and stuff so.

00:01:14.327 --> 00:01:15.947
- [Interviewer] And
Tasha, tell me about your,

00:01:15.947 --> 00:01:17.260
how you grew up

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.653
- Pretty much had the same type of family.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.720
Dad wasn't around mom wasn't
really around much either.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.350
Went to Kansas for a while.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.183
Being,

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.000
I was emancipated.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.640
I started cooking drugs
before I did drugs.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.000
I was making drugs at six years old

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.763
and I didn't start doing
drugs since I was almost 30.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.550
And then when I did do
drugs, I was spent hard on.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.470
Real hard.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.690
It was mainly

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.870
it was everything I would do
would have to be in a needle.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:45.703
It wasn't in a needle.

00:01:45.703 --> 00:01:46.710
I wasn't gonna do it.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.660
I raised my brother.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.170
- [Interviewer] How was,
how was your childhood?

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.430
Any traumatic events?

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.312
- Yeah, it was, yeah.

00:01:58.312 --> 00:01:59.970
Real traumatic events.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.810
Being in a biker family being a girl

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.810
isn't all that it seems it should be.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.093
It's nearly not that.

00:02:05.972 --> 00:02:07.222
It's ain't fun.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.810
You think it's fun at the
time, but it's not fun.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.066
- [Interviewer] So abuse of what sort?

00:02:12.066 --> 00:02:13.070
- Yeah.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.050
- [Interviewer] Violent?

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:14.980
- Yeah.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.210
- [Interviewer] Sexual abuse?

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.230
- Yeah my ex-husband had me kidnapped.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.340
He kidnapped me and kept me secluded

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.320
from my family for three years.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.203
I couldn't talk to them.

00:02:24.203 --> 00:02:28.314
I had two kids in that time
who they didn't get to see.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.363
And then they finally got to see later on.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.676
- [Interviewer] How far
do you guys go in school?

00:02:34.676 --> 00:02:38.820
- I ended up getting my high
school equivalency in prison

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.643
but I made it in school to ninth grade.

00:02:40.643 --> 00:02:41.476
- [Interviewer] Ninth grade?

00:02:41.476 --> 00:02:42.309
- Yeah.
- Same here, ninth grade.

00:02:42.309 --> 00:02:43.340
- [Interviewer] Ninth grade.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.173
- First day, ninth grade.

00:02:44.173 --> 00:02:46.133
- [Interviewer] And
then you guys met, how?

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:47.885
- He took my job.

00:02:47.885 --> 00:02:51.430
- Yeah, I took her job as
a manager at a call center

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.638
and we're doing really
well, got a house, a car-

00:02:56.638 --> 00:02:58.290
- Nice house, had my kids.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.320
- Yeah, we were doing well, and then

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.950
an event took place in the front
yard of our house and ended

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:13.370
up losing my job, my house, my
ID, everything at that point.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.640
- Kids.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.620
- So we decided to go on
vacation to California.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.453
Boom!

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.410
Came out here.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.810
And once we came out

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.050
to California the series
of unfortunate events

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:30.050
just continued like cascaded
into a year on Skid row.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.130
- [Interviewer] So tell me
about your year on Skid row.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.664
- [Tasha] Mine, I enjoyed it.

00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:36.497
I, actually did.

00:03:36.497 --> 00:03:37.330
I didn't have,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.220
I stayed at the rescue mission
for about three months.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.750
Union rescue mission.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.100
- [Interviewer] Union rescue
mission is one of the big,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.009
bigger missions here.

00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:45.547
- [Tasha] Yeah, right
there on Skid row yeah.

00:03:45.547 --> 00:03:48.820
And then I went from there
when the COVID came out

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.930
I got me a tent and sat
up on third and main.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.460
And that was crazy.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.293
That,

00:03:56.293 --> 00:03:58.340
that was crazy.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.950
And then they figured a hotel for a while.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.010
I was there for about two
months, till you got here

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.190
and then once he got here,
I forfeited the hotel.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.011
Cause he couldn't stay there me.

00:04:07.011 --> 00:04:08.722
- [Jason] I got here and

00:04:08.722 --> 00:04:10.693
the homeless had taken over,

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:12.783
not Grand park.

00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:13.616
- [Tasha] Except for riots.

00:04:13.616 --> 00:04:15.030
- [Jason] But the park,

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.694
What is it, Central park?

00:04:16.694 --> 00:04:17.640
- [Tasha] Grand beach, Grand park.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.470
- [Jason] Grand park.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.110
A black lives matter group had taken

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.740
over that park entirely.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.000
It was like living there.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.640
And there were riots every
night, like helicopters

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.930
with spotlights and

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.030
goon squad up and down the streets.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:33.863
It was crazy.

00:04:33.863 --> 00:04:35.070
- [Tasha] It was in the
LA Times, front page.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.920
- [Jason] I got my jaw shattered
the first day I was here.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.460
I lost track of her and
was lost in downtown

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.320
like three in the morning
I'm yelling for her,

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.700
and like out of nowhere I get surrounded

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.010
like kicked up off the ground

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.610
by a horseshoe bike lock
hits me right in my jaw.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.420
- [Interviewer] So who shattered your jaw?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.121
- [Jason] Some really,
really huge black dudes.

00:04:54.121 --> 00:04:54.954
(laughing)

00:04:54.954 --> 00:04:57.810
Like it's three buddies, but like, yeah.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.330
- [Interviewer] And was there
something you were doing that?

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.477
- No, no.

00:05:00.477 --> 00:05:01.433
- He was at third and main

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:03.370
- I was just looking, looking
like I had a little bit

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.203
of money
- Yelling for me.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.030
- And yelling for her
at three in the morning.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:06.863
- Where I used to stay.

00:05:06.863 --> 00:05:09.593
- Yeah I was completely oblivious

00:05:09.593 --> 00:05:11.550
to the fact that I was in the projects

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.149
running around screaming
for my white girlfriend.

00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:14.982
(laughing)

00:05:14.982 --> 00:05:15.930
And then I was like, yeah

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.840
like I now looking back,
I know it was ridiculous.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.673
- [Interviewer] So you guys,

00:05:19.673 --> 00:05:20.510
you guys lived in a tent?

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:21.486
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:21.486 --> 00:05:23.420
- [Interviewer] I just found
you at the Greyhound station.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.630
You're getting ready
to go back to Missouri.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.430
- Yeah, you found us on the last day

00:05:27.986 --> 00:05:31.679
of our craziest adventure
we've ever been on.

00:05:31.679 --> 00:05:33.077
- [Interviewer] What kind
of stuff have you seen

00:05:33.077 --> 00:05:33.910
in your time here?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.399
- Oh man, we have saved,

00:05:35.399 --> 00:05:37.300
several people's lives.
- I have saved people's lives.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.683
- Seen several people die.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:43.003
- I seen this dead lady in
this tent all screwed up

00:05:43.003 --> 00:05:46.190
looking like this and some
dude doing some voodoo stuff.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.350
It was,

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:48.183
wild.

00:05:48.183 --> 00:05:49.016
She was old.

00:05:49.016 --> 00:05:51.610
I mean, she was been dead for awhile,

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.540
for a long while.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.373
- Yeah.

00:05:54.373 --> 00:05:55.490
- It was creepy.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:56.515
- You see things out here.

00:05:56.515 --> 00:05:58.699
They're like, they're
not even human anymore.

00:05:58.699 --> 00:05:59.532
They don't even don't-

00:05:59.532 --> 00:06:01.010
- That chick that was
slamming her head on the tree?

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.230
- Yeah.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.320
There was this chick.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.930
She was just completely possessed

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.037
to a point where she didn't feel no

00:06:08.037 --> 00:06:09.770
no real pain at all.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.250
She's slapping her head off this tree.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.600
- And you just hear-

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.433
- Yeah.

00:06:13.433 --> 00:06:14.440
- And there's laughing.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.750
- Sickening thud every
time she slaps her head

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.352
off this tree and then she just laughs

00:06:19.352 --> 00:06:20.410
and like rips chunk of her hair out.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.877
And-

00:06:21.877 --> 00:06:22.710
- Right in front of our tent.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:23.543
- Yeah, I'm like what in the hell?

00:06:23.543 --> 00:06:25.100
- And I tried to grab my clothes.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.880
- And she's like 20 years
old and kind of pretty,

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.713
ad you're just like.

00:06:27.713 --> 00:06:28.870
- Like what happened?

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.128
- I'm like what happened to you?

00:06:31.128 --> 00:06:32.800
- But then months later she was normal.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.180
- Yeah, completely normal.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:35.013
Like it was never happening.

00:06:35.013 --> 00:06:36.020
- Yeah.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.530
- [Interviewer] So what
drugs do you guys play

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.363
around with now?

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.360
- Well I play around just a
little bit of anything, but.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.410
- I just do meth and I smoke lots of weed,

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:46.285
- I smoke tons of weed.

00:06:46.285 --> 00:06:47.118
- Lots of weed.

00:06:47.118 --> 00:06:48.433
- [Interviewer] And how do
you guys support yourself?

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:50.860
- Pretty much out here.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.630
It's through little, little
bit of selling of drugs

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.670
by enough to where I can
sell a little bit and pay

00:06:57.670 --> 00:06:59.310
for my addiction really
and that's about it.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.550
Everything else gets fed to us.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:02.700
- [Interviewer] And Tasha,
are you doing what a lot

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.400
of the ladies do sometimes?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.763
- Yeah, I just I sell drags a lot.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.376
Meth out here is like cash.

00:07:10.376 --> 00:07:11.280
If you got meth you can
have anything you want.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.282
- [Interviewer] No but
what I was referring to is

00:07:14.282 --> 00:07:15.860
do you date guys for money?

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:16.693
- No.

00:07:16.693 --> 00:07:17.990
- [Interviewer] You don't?

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:21.050
- Everybody thinks that she does though.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.172
Yeah I know.

00:07:22.172 --> 00:07:23.005
- The way I dress.

00:07:23.005 --> 00:07:24.473
- And she chooses to dress like this too.

00:07:26.224 --> 00:07:28.240
- This is like calm compared
to what I usually wear.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.304
- It gets me in a lot of fights.

00:07:29.304 --> 00:07:31.300
(laughing)

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.690
- Yeah.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:33.600
- I like to dress creative.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.510
- [Interviewer] Do
either of you have kids?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.040
- Yeah, we both do.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.228
- Yeah, I've got three kids.

00:07:37.228 --> 00:07:38.061
- I've got two.
- But none together.

00:07:38.061 --> 00:07:39.522
- I've got two, none together though.

00:07:39.522 --> 00:07:40.430
- [Interviewer] None together?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.263
- No.

00:07:41.263 --> 00:07:42.873
- [Interviewer] And
who's raising your kids.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.400
- My daughter's mom.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.050
- And my kids are staying
with my stepmom and my dad.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.200
- [Interviewer] And so, yeah,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.347
So you'll go back to Missouri and do what?

00:07:53.347 --> 00:07:54.310
- I'm going back to see my kids.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.460
Yeah, I'm going back to see
my father before he dies.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:59.110
Actually he's in a retirement home

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:01.530
even though we had a rough childhood

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.910
he's still my hero and he was a great man.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.950
So I just don't, I don't blame him

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.730
for it because I don't
think he knew any better.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:09.563
I just think it was just

00:08:09.563 --> 00:08:11.255
he was a product of his environment.

00:08:11.255 --> 00:08:13.405
- [Interviewer] You have to
understand that these people

00:08:13.405 --> 00:08:16.254
that we all see as guilty,

00:08:16.254 --> 00:08:17.087
- Yeah.

00:08:17.087 --> 00:08:17.989
- [Interviewer] Probably went through

00:08:17.989 --> 00:08:18.822
something equally bad or worse?

00:08:18.822 --> 00:08:19.655
- Exactly, exactly.

00:08:19.655 --> 00:08:20.488
- Or worse yeah.

00:08:20.488 --> 00:08:22.720
- Cause, if I was to be mad at him

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.345
then I'd have to be mad at
myself too, because I did

00:08:25.345 --> 00:08:27.120
I've done the same thing to my daughter.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.633
- [Interviewer] Forgiveness is the answer.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:32.600
What was the most important
lesson you guys have learned?

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.690
- Don't take anything for granted.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.113
Don't have value on things.

00:08:36.113 --> 00:08:37.838
- Don't get caught up on material things.

00:08:37.838 --> 00:08:39.190
- And possessions.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.670
- Cause material things,
aren't what matters.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.503
- It isn't.

00:08:42.503 --> 00:08:43.400
- It's not what you got it's who you got.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.660
- And your word.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.256
And we say "you going do something

00:08:47.256 --> 00:08:48.089
and so you're gonna do
something make sure you go

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:49.000
through with it."

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.840
You know

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.673
- Yup.

00:08:50.673 --> 00:08:52.500
I've had some of the best
times of my life out here

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.330
on Skid row and definitely
had some of the worst.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.900
- If somebody needs
something and you got it,

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.417
give it to him, man.

00:08:58.417 --> 00:09:00.062
If you can give it to him give it him man.

00:09:00.062 --> 00:09:00.895
- There are some of the coolest,

00:09:00.895 --> 00:09:02.010
realest, nicest people out here.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:02.843
- Really.

00:09:02.843 --> 00:09:05.180
- For real, they will do anything for you.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.405
- But at the same time there's
people there that would-

00:09:07.405 --> 00:09:08.238
- They'll play the role.

00:09:08.238 --> 00:09:10.090
- And take everything you got.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.410
- Yeah.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.510
And kick you in the nuts.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.399
- Yeah.

00:09:13.399 --> 00:09:14.232
( interviewer laughing)

00:09:14.232 --> 00:09:15.450
- We've had our tent burn down twice.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.283
- Yeah.

00:09:16.283 --> 00:09:17.116
- I had mine ripped apart

00:09:17.116 --> 00:09:21.300
by the protestors and pee
thrown at me and spit on.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.200
Cause I was white.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.350
I was on third main.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.010
- [Interviewer] How was
your year here changed you?

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.507
- My jaw is shaped a little different now.

00:09:28.507 --> 00:09:29.431
(laughing)

00:09:29.431 --> 00:09:31.763
- I'm a little bit more bossy.

00:09:34.024 --> 00:09:35.890
I'm really independent now I
know if I could make it here

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:40.750
in California and on Skid
row so I can be anywhere.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:44.050
- Now when people approach me,
I'm not necessarily so nice

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.200
at first I used to

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.420
welcome anybody.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.570
Like I wanted to talk to anybody.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.000
I was a salesman and
that's what I love to do,

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.270
I'd talk to anybody.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:55.237
Now when people approach me I'm like,

00:09:55.237 --> 00:09:56.070
- "what do you want?"

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:56.903
- Yeah.

00:09:56.903 --> 00:09:57.900
Like "step back,

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.632
give me six feet or I'm
going to freak out."

00:10:00.632 --> 00:10:02.173
What the hell do you want?

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.380
- He doesn't quite like the
way I dress so much anymore.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.560
- It messed me up.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:07.790
It was a traumatic experience.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.540
Getting my teeth knocked out like that.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.070
I didn't even go to the
hospital for my jaw.

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:11.903
I was too scared.

00:10:11.903 --> 00:10:13.340
I was like, "nope".

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:16.260
I fell asleep that night
wrapped around a bush up front

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.870
of the hospital because I
went to go into the hospital

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.480
and like when I walked
through the door, I'm like

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:22.680
I'm covering my mouth and-

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.470
Cause this is before
face masks were real bad

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.740
and I'm covering my mouth.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:29.080
And I was like, they're
like, "can we help you?"

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:29.913
I'm like,

00:10:29.913 --> 00:10:32.090
"I gotta go get my wife
out of the car real quick."

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.180
And I ran back out and
hid around a bush and

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:35.840
I still hadn't even found
her until the next day

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:39.320
when I walked like four
miles still completely lost.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.153
Fuckin',

00:10:40.153 --> 00:10:40.986
yeah.

00:10:40.986 --> 00:10:41.950
- That was actually where I took him.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.700
- Yeah I was like four blocks from

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.390
where I was supposed to be.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.690
But in LA that's a big deal

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:49.260
especially when you're not from here.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:50.743
I had no idea where I was.

00:10:51.579 --> 00:10:52.900
It was horrible.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.460
It definitely put up all

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:58.630
shields.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.480
- Relationships don't
really last out here.

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:01.380
- I was like red alert to the fullest.

00:11:02.238 --> 00:11:03.742
No new relationships don't
really last on Skid row.

00:11:03.742 --> 00:11:05.838
- People give us crap all
the time like cause we fight.

00:11:05.838 --> 00:11:06.830
- Everybody, everybody hates the fact that

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:07.929
we're together because
nobody has a lasting

00:11:07.929 --> 00:11:11.668
relationship out here, they're
just pass roaming around.

00:11:11.668 --> 00:11:12.501
- With a faithful girlfriend.

00:11:12.501 --> 00:11:13.580
- [Interviewer] I think once drugs become

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.670
part of the picture
your priorities change.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.763
- Yeah absolutely.

00:11:16.763 --> 00:11:17.910
- I was gonna say the same.

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:18.980
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:19.813
- We're faithful to each other.

00:11:19.813 --> 00:11:21.140
- [Interviewer] It's
remarkable that you guys are

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:21.973
stayed together.

00:11:21.973 --> 00:11:22.806
- Yeah, yeah.

00:11:22.806 --> 00:11:23.639
- I love him.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.410
- Both of us have already been conquered

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:30.880
by drugs once and like kind of now,

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.500
now we just use drugs

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.300
because that's literally
what we've always done.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:38.860
It's a form of self-medicating,
but really I can't function

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:42.900
unless I do use drugs to at
least a small extent I've used

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.350
at least a little bit of drugs or else

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.401
then I'm not able to function.

00:11:46.401 --> 00:11:47.770
Like, I don't know,

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:52.770
I've always worked a good
job and been on drugs.

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:55.400
Like, I mean, to some extent.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.000
Of course every time I get
too far out there on drugs,

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.080
I lose my job and everything, but.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.450
- I quit doing drugs for a whole lot.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.680
- Yeah, Yeah.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:03.513
Both of us do.

00:12:03.513 --> 00:12:04.840
We'll quit using the drug

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.270
if we, if we start using it too much

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:07.670
we'll stop for a little while.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.160
And it's always at different times too.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.600
So it's really weird the
way, the way it works.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.280
Well then just quit shooting up.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.130
She quit like five months ago.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.540
Yeah.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.835
- We're only still doing it
and I'm like, "Nope, I'm done."

00:12:19.835 --> 00:12:20.877
I don't wanna do like that no more.

00:12:20.877 --> 00:12:22.410
I'll smoke it down but.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:23.450
- [Interviewer] Do you guys feel like your

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:25.850
the childhood environments
or the families you grew

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:26.974
up in kind of

00:12:26.974 --> 00:12:28.877
- I grantee it.
- Absolutely.

00:12:28.877 --> 00:12:30.210
- [Interviewer] Put you
where you are today?

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.043
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:33.060
- [Jason] Shaped us for it
because there's, there's no way

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.580
a normal person is going
to get just dropped

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.440
off out here and be okay.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.273
There's no way.

00:12:37.273 --> 00:12:39.130
- [Tasha] You can make
Skid row being a female,

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:42.490
a white female by yourself

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.410
and sell drugs and live where I lived.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.230
It's, I'm surprised.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:49.063
Everything bad that's happened to me.

00:12:49.063 --> 00:12:49.896
- [Jason] I've had a fight like four

00:12:49.896 --> 00:12:51.206
or five times in one day
before because of it.

00:12:51.206 --> 00:12:52.710
- [Tasha] Because of me.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.663
- [Jason] Yeah, because
her, yeah, it's ridiculous.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:57.553
- [Interviewer] All right you guys,

00:12:57.553 --> 00:12:59.371
I'll take you back to the bus station.

00:12:59.371 --> 00:13:00.204
- [Tasha] All right.
- [Jason] All right cool.

00:13:00.204 --> 00:13:01.037
- [Interviewer] Where
you can get your bus.

00:13:01.037 --> 00:13:01.870
Thank you so much.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:03.453
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

